<title>ESTONIA: EMV CUM-STOCK DIVIDEND TRADING TO END.</title>
<headline>EMV CUM-STOCK DIVIDEND TRADING TO END.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade in EMV shares, one of Estonia's largest construction companies, will be ex-dividend from April 25, the Tallinn stock exchange (TSE) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Today, April 24, is the last day for cum-stock dividend trading in EMV shares,&quot; the TSE said in a statement.</p>
<p>Thursday is also the last day for trade with the right to participate in the company's stock dividend issue. The company will issue one share for every share held.</p>
<p>--Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
